            <ArticleTitle>Unfractionated and low-molecular-weight heparins in acute coronary syndromes: current recommendations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-65</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>All patients with acute coronary syndromes and without obvious bleeding or acute cerebrovascular events are candidates for heparin therapy. This article is a review of the pharmacology of unfractionated and low-molecular-weight heparins, trials of heparin therapy in acute coronary syndromes, and recommendations for using these agents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
